{"absent":["Locking, concurrency and calling context rules for early mapping and table parsing are not shown.","Values for protection key access and write inhibitions are not given.","Semantics of debug control words, performance sampling, streaming mode entry, key management and guarded stack faults are not shown.","ACPI interpreter behavior, PCI scanning and interrupt setup beyond enable flags are not shown.","Detailed error strings, hibernation signature width and boot graphics parsing are not shown."],"dossier":"D11","findings":[{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/kvm.h::KVM_ARM_FEATURE_ID_RANGE_IDX","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/kvm.h::KVM_ARM_FEATURE_ID_RANGE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/kvm.h::KVM_ARM_FEATURE_ID_RANGE_SIZE"],"text":"The virtualization header defines feature range zero with capacity for three groups of eight by eight entries. The index key folds the four valued operation field into three values then packs that result with the low three bits of the middle selector and the low three bits of the final selector."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/kvm.h::reg_mask_range"],"text":"A mask range descriptor pairs an eight byte address locating a mask array with a four byte range selector and thirteen spare four byte words."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/mman.h::PROT_BTI","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/mman.h::PROT_MTE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/mman.h::PKEY_DISABLE_EXECUTE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/mman.h::PKEY_DISABLE_READ","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/mman.h::PKEY_ACCESS_MASK"],"text":"Branch target guarded pages use protection value 0x10 while tagged mappings use 0x20. Key based execute inhibition is 0x4 and read inhibition is 0x8, with the combined access mask aggregating the access, write, read and execute inhibitions."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/param.h::__ASM_PARAM_H","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/param.h::EXEC_PAGESIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/setup.h::COMMAND_LINE_SIZE"],"text":"Execution page size is 65536 bytes and the command line limit is 2048 bytes."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/perf_regs.h::_ASM_ARM64_PERF_REGS_H","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/perf_regs.h::perf_event_arm_regs","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/perf_regs.h::PERF_REG_EXTENDED_MASK"],"text":"Performance sampling names general registers X0 through X28 consecutively, then link register, stack pointer, program counter and a maximum sentinel. The vector granule pseudo register is at position 46 and its extended mask is a single bit derived from that position."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/posix_types.h::__ASM_POSIX_TYPES_H","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/posix_types.h::__kernel_old_uid_t.alt_1","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/posix_types.h::__kernel_old_gid_t","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/posix_types.h::__kernel_old_uid_t.alt_2"],"text":"Legacy user and group identifiers are each an unsigned short quantity, with a self alias macro for the user type."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_MODE_EL0t","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_MODE_EL1t","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_MODE_EL1h","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_MODE_EL2t","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_MODE_EL2h","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_MODE_EL3t","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_MODE_EL3h","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_MODE_MASK","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_MODE32_BIT"],"text":"Exception level and thread state occupy the low nibble masked by 0xf. Encodings are zero for level zero thread, 0x4 and 0x5 for level one thread and handler, 0x8 and 0x9 for level two, 0xc and 0xd for level three, with 32 bit mode flagged by 0x10."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_F_BIT","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_I_BIT","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_A_BIT","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_D_BIT","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_BTYPE_MASK","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_SSBS_BIT","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_PAN_BIT","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_UAO_BIT","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_DIT_BIT","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_TCO_BIT","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_V_BIT","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_C_BIT","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_Z_BIT","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_N_BIT","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_BTYPE_SHIFT","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_f","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_s","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_x","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_c","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_BTYPE_NONE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_BTYPE_JC","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_BTYPE_C","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PSR_BTYPE_J"],"text":"Interrupt and control bits are F at 0x40, I at 0x80, A at 0x100, D at 0x200, single step state at 0x1000, access never at 0x400000, override at 0x800000, timing at 0x1000000 and tag check at 0x2000000, with condition flags V, C, Z, N at the top nibble. Branch type uses two bits at shift 10 masked by 0xc00 with four encodings for none and combinations of jump and call. The word is also viewed as flag, status, extension and control bytes."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PTRACE_SYSEMU","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PTRACE_SYSEMU_SINGLESTEP","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PTRACE_PEEKMTETAGS","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::PTRACE_POKEMTETAGS"],"text":"System call emulation uses request 31 with single step variant 32, while tag memory access uses 33 for read and 34 for write."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::user_pt_regs","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::user_fpsimd_state","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::user_hwdebug_state","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::user_hwdebug_state.anon_1"],"text":"General state exposes thirty one eight byte registers plus stack pointer, program counter and processor state. Vector state holds thirty two sixteen byte slots plus status, control and spare words. Debug state carries an info word with padding and sixteen address plus control pairs."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::user_sve_header","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::user_za_header"],"text":"Vector and matrix headers each store total meaningful size and maximum size, current and maximum vector length, a flags half word and a reserved half word."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_REGS_MASK","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_REGS_FPSIMD","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_REGS_SVE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_VL_INHERIT","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_VL_ONEXEC","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::ZA_PT_VL_INHERIT","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::ZA_PT_VL_ONEXEC"],"text":"One low flag bit distinguishes floating point view zero from vector view one. Vector length inheritance and on exec controls are the upper half of the corresponding process control bits for both vector and matrix extensions."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_REGS_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_FPSIMD_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_FPSIMD_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_SVE_ZREG_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_SVE_PREG_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_SVE_FFR_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_SVE_FPSR_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_SVE_FPCR_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_SVE_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_SVE_ZREGS_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_SVE_ZREG_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_SVE_ZREGS_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_SVE_PREGS_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_SVE_PREG_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_SVE_PREGS_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_SVE_FFR_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_SVE_FPSR_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_SVE_FPCR_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_SVE_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::SVE_PT_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::ZA_PT_ZA_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::ZA_PT_ZAV_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::ZA_PT_ZA_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::ZA_PT_SIZE"],"text":"Ptrace vector payloads begin at header size rounded up to quadword granularity. Floating point view has fixed size at that start, while vector view sequences data registers, predicate registers, fault register, then status and control words with per register and aggregate sizing and total rounded to granularity. Matrix data follows a similarly aligned header with square tile sizing and row stride scaled by vector length."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::user_pac_mask","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::user_pac_address_keys","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::user_pac_generic_keys","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::user_gcs"],"text":"Masking state holds separate eight byte data and instruction masks. Address keys group four sixteen byte values for instruction and data pairs, the generic key is one sixteen byte value, and guarded stack state holds enabled features, locked features and the current pointer."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::sigcontext","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ucontext.h::ucontext"],"text":"Signal context starts with fault address, thirty one registers, stack pointer, program counter and processor state, then four kilobytes of sixteen byte aligned reserve. User context chains flags, link, stack and mask with padding to a fixed large size, ending with that signal context."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::_aarch64_ctx","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::fpsimd_context","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::esr_context","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::poe_context","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::extra_context","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::sve_context","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::tpidr2_context","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::fpmr_context","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::za_context","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::zt_context","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::gcs_context"],"text":"Each signal extension begins with magic and size. Bodies then carry floating status with vectors, exception syndrome, overlay permission, an aligned out of line pointer with size, vector length with flags, thread pointer, floating mode, matrix length, tile count, and guarded stack pointer with features."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::FPSIMD_MAGIC","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::ESR_MAGIC","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::POE_MAGIC","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::EXTRA_MAGIC","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::SVE_MAGIC","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::SVE_SIG_FLAG_SM","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::TPIDR2_MAGIC","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::FPMR_MAGIC","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::ZA_MAGIC","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::ZT_MAGIC","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::GCS_MAGIC"],"text":"Magics are 0x46508001 for floating point, 0x45535201 for syndrome, 0x504f4530 for overlay, 0x45585401 for extra, 0x53564501 for vector, 0x54504902 for thread pointer, 0x46504d52 for floating mode, 0x54366345 for matrix, 0x5a544e01 for tile and 0x47435300 for guarded stack, with low bit 0x1 marking streaming mode."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sve_context.h::__SVE_VQ_BYTES","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sve_context.h::__SVE_VQ_MIN","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sve_context.h::__SVE_VQ_MAX","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sve_context.h::__SVE_VL_MIN","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sve_context.h::__SVE_VL_MAX","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sve_context.h::__SVE_NUM_ZREGS","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sve_context.h::__SVE_NUM_PREGS","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sve_context.h::__sve_vl_valid","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sve_context.h::__sve_vq_from_vl","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sve_context.h::__sve_vl_from_vq","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::SVE_VQ_BYTES","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::SVE_VQ_MIN","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::SVE_VQ_MAX","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::SVE_VL_MIN","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::SVE_VL_MAX","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::SVE_NUM_ZREGS","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::SVE_NUM_PREGS","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::sve_vl_valid","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::sve_vl_from_vq"],"text":"One quadword is 16 bytes with count from 1 to 512 and byte length by scaling. Thirty two data and sixteen predicate registers are provided, with length valid only when aligned and within bounds, plus conversions between count and bytes."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sve_context.h::__SVE_ZREG_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sve_context.h::__SVE_PREG_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sve_context.h::__SVE_FFR_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sve_context.h::__SVE_ZREGS_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sve_context.h::__SVE_ZREG_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sve_context.h::__SVE_ZREGS_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sve_context.h::__SVE_PREGS_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sve_context.h::__SVE_PREG_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sve_context.h::__SVE_PREGS_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sve_context.h::__SVE_FFR_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::SVE_SIG_ZREG_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::SVE_SIG_PREG_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::SVE_SIG_FFR_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::SVE_SIG_REGS_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::SVE_SIG_ZREGS_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::SVE_SIG_ZREG_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::SVE_SIG_ZREGS_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::SVE_SIG_PREGS_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::SVE_SIG_PREG_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::SVE_SIG_PREGS_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::SVE_SIG_FFR_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::SVE_SIG_CONTEXT_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::ZA_SIG_REGS_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::ZA_SIG_ZAV_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::ZA_SIG_CONTEXT_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::ZT_SIG_REG_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::ZT_SIG_REG_BYTES","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::ZT_SIG_REGS_OFFSET","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::ZT_SIG_REGS_SIZE","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::ZT_SIG_CONTEXT_SIZE"],"text":"Signal vector layout rounds its header to quadword granularity, then orders data registers from zero, predicates after data, fault register after predicates, with per register and aggregate helpers and total including header. Matrix rows scale by register size and tile metadata uses fixed 512 bit units counted in bytes."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/signal.h::SA_RESTORER","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/signal.h::MINSIGSTKSZ","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/signal.h::SIGSTKSZ","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/statfs.h::__ASM_STATFS_H","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/statfs.h::ARCH_PACK_COMPAT_STATFS64"],"text":"Restore flag is 0x04000000 with minimum stack 5120 and default 16384 bytes. Compatibility filesystem statistics are packed and four byte aligned."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/mman.h::_UAPI__ASM_MMAN_H","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/param.h::__ASM_PARAM_H","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/perf_regs.h::_ASM_ARM64_PERF_REGS_H","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/posix_types.h::__ASM_POSIX_TYPES_H","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ptrace.h::_UAPI__ASM_PTRACE_H","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/setup.h::__ASM_SETUP_H","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sigcontext.h::_UAPI__ASM_SIGCONTEXT_H","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/signal.h::__ASM_SIGNAL_H","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/statfs.h::__ASM_STATFS_H","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/sve_context.h::_UAPI__ASM_SVE_CONTEXT_H","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/ucontext.h::_UAPI__ASM_UCONTEXT_H"],"text":"Public headers use include sentinels to allow safe repeated inclusion."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/arm64/kernel/acpi.c::__acpi_map_table","arch/arm64/kernel/acpi.c::__acpi_unmap_table"],"text":"Early table mapping declines empty sizes and otherwise creates a temporary mapping, with release safely ignoring absent or empty inputs."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/arm64/kernel/acpi.c::acpi_psci_use_hvc"],"text":"A predicate reports whether firmware boot flags select hypervisor call transport for power coordination."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/kernel/acpi.c::pr_fmt","arch/arm64/kernel/acpi.c::acpi_noirq","arch/arm64/kernel/acpi.c::acpi_disabled","arch/arm64/kernel/acpi.c::acpi_pci_disabled"],"text":"Log lines from this unit carry a firmware prefix and interrupt, general and PCI firmware handling all start disabled."},{"kind":"state_machine","sids":["arch/arm64/kernel/acpi.c::__initdata.alt_1","arch/arm64/kernel/acpi.c::__initdata.alt_2","arch/arm64/kernel/acpi.c::__initdata.alt_3","arch/arm64/kernel/acpi.c::__initdata.alt_4","arch/arm64/kernel/acpi.c::parse_acpi","arch/arm64/kernel/acpi.c::dt_is_stub","arch/arm64/kernel/acpi.c::acpi_fadt_sanity_check","arch/arm64/kernel/acpi.c::acpi_boot_table_init"],"text":"Firmware control accepts off, on, force and console suppression and rejects other values. Only a reservation node plus optional hypervisor node counts as stub device tree. Tables load unless off or unless a non stub tree exists without on or force. Load enables the subsystem, validates tables, disables again on failure unless forced, then selects early console, hibernation signature and graphics handling by enabled state."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/kernel/acpi.c::acpi_fadt_sanity_check"],"text":"Description table must exist and meet revision five point one, with older tables accepted only when arm boot flags are present amid a warning. Hardware reduced mode is required and the acquired reference is always released."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["arch/arm64/kernel/acpi.c::acpi_boot_table_init"],"text":"Firmware table initialization runs early at boot to decide between firmware and device tree and to establish console and graphics state."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["arch/arm64/kernel/acpi.c::acpi_fadt_sanity_check","arch/arm64/kernel/acpi.c::acpi_boot_table_init","arch/arm64/kernel/acpi.c::__acpi_map_table"],"text":"Missing tables, old revisions without compatibility flags, or full hardware mode fall back to device tree unless forced. Empty mapping and release requests are ignored instead of faulting."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/printk.h::pr_err"],"text":"External diagnostic reporting facility owned elsewhere."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/acpi.h::acpi_parse_spcr"],"text":"External serial console table parser owned elsewhere."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/acpi.h::acpi_table_parse"],"text":"External generic table parser owned elsewhere."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/kconfi